**Where Digital Can Be Observed**

Observable digital practice across the Six Stages of Learning  ·  Weston College Group  ·  2025–26

| **Learning Intentions** |
| --- |
| ◦  Learning intention is clear, shared and connects to prior learning |
| ◦  Success criteria are explicit — learners know what good looks like |
| ◦  Intention is revisited or checked during the session |
| **◈  **Intention visible digitally — posted in Teams, on screen or in the channel before learners arrive |
| **◈  **Success criteria linked to assignment brief or rubric in Teams |
| **Building Blocks** |
| ◦  Session builds logically on prior learning — sequence is deliberate |
| ◦  Resources are prepared and available before the session starts |
| ◦  Differentiation is planned, not improvised |
| **◈  **Teams channel structure mirrors the curriculum sequence — learners can navigate their own learning |
| **◈  **Previous session materials are findable without asking the teacher |
| **◈  **Resources are accessible by design — alt text, heading structure, readable fonts — before sharing, not after |
| **Starting Points** |
| ◦  Teacher knows where learners are starting from and uses this to adapt delivery |
| ◦  Initial assessment has informed planning or grouping |
| ◦  Learners with SEND or additional needs have appropriate adjustments in place |
| **◈  **Digital diagnostic used to establish baseline — Century, Forms quiz, or equivalent |
| **◈  **Diagnostic data is visible in session design — not just filed away |
| **◈  **Assistive technology is offered proactively, not only when a learner asks |
| **Activities** |
| ◦  Learners are active — thinking, doing, constructing — not just receiving |
| ◦  Modelling makes expert thinking visible, not just the finished product |
| ◦  Collaborative activity is structured purposefully — learners know why they are working together |
| ◦  Learners have genuine choice in how they respond or demonstrate understanding |
| **◈  **Collaborative document, shared whiteboard or poll used so all learners' thinking is visible simultaneously |
| **◈  **Screen recording, annotation or digital pen captures teacher thinking — available for learners after the session |
| **◈  **Multiple response formats offered — written, video, audio, annotated image — chosen to match the task |
| **◈  **Learners use AI as a thinking tool — to generate questions, identify gaps, or test understanding — not to replace thinking |
| **Assessment** |
| ◦  A hinge point is used before moving on — teacher checks understanding, not just coverage |
| ◦  Questioning stretches thinking — open, probing, building on responses |
| ◦  Assessment informs what happens next in the session — teacher adapts |
| ◦  Peer or self-assessment is structured — learners know what they are looking for |
| **◈  **Poll, Forms quiz or Mentimeter used as hinge point — results visible and acted on in the moment |
| **◈  **Feedback given during the task via annotation, audio comment or Grades tab — learners can act on it while the work is live |
| **Lasting Learning** |
| ◦  Retrieval practice is built into the session — learners generate from memory, not recognition |
| ◦  There is evidence of learning across sessions, not just within this one |
| ◦  Learners can access and act on their learning independently after the session ends |
| **◈  **Session recording or worked example is embedded in the Teams resource — learners can replay expert thinking |
| **◈  **Channel is organised so a learner who missed the session can find everything without contacting the teacher |
| **◈  **AT tools are accessible without staff intervention — supporting independence, revision and recall |
| ◦  TLA practice       **◈  Digital opportunity**  — present where the teacher has chosen digital; not a requirement where they haven't. |

*Digital supports and enhances exceptional TLA practice. It does not replace it. The question is always: what is the rationale, and what is the expected impact on learning?*

Graeme Wright  ·  Digital Pedagogy Coach  ·  Quality & Innovation  ·  Weston College  ·  June 2026